{:edb/db-before-t 1382 :edb/db-after-t 1383 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534695 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:25:30.677Z" 13194139534695 true] [17592186092329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303857 13194139534695 true] [17592186092329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303860 13194139534695 true] [17592186092330 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303850 13194139534695 true] [17592186092330 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303864 13194139534695 true] [17592186092453 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534695 true] [17592186092453 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534695 false] [17592186092453 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = \\frac{4}{x^{3}} - x$ at the point $(1, 3)$." 13194139534695 false] [17592186092453 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-x$ at the point $(1,3).$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186092453 1145 "Differentiate $f(x)=4x^{-3}-x$ to get $f'(x)=-12x^{-4}-1$. At $x=1$, the slope is $-13$. Use the point $(1,3)$:\n$$y-3=-13(x-1),\\qquad y=-13x+16.$$" 13194139534695 false] [17592186092453 1145 "Let $f(x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-12{x}^{-4}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=-12(1)^{-4}-1=-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-13$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,3),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(3) & =-13(x-1) \\\\ y & =-13x+13+3 \\\\ y & =-13x+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303850 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303851 13194139534695 true] [17592186303850 1089 "q-10830" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303850 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534695 true] [17592186303850 1100 "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}-4x$ at  $(1,0)$ intersects the $y$-axis." 13194139534695 true] [17592186303850 1113 #uuid "69a37f15-9ffb-5f60-8272-1cb813acb27b" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303850 1145 "Let $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}-4x.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}-4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{1/2}-4x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=2(1)^{-1/2}-4=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(0) & =-2(x-1) \\\\ y & =-2x+2-0 \\\\ y & =-2x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2(0)+2=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $(0,2).$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303852 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303853 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303854 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303855 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303856 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1041 "selection" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303855 13194139534695 true] [17592186303851 1110 #uuid "92d1386b-d3db-590b-801c-7530ed893c12" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303852 1034 "(0,0)" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303852 1111 #uuid "84d78aa0-b6ec-553b-82a1-412fa0407777" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303853 1034 "(0,1)" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303853 1111 #uuid "a0355a81-9cb0-5381-8817-9e61f963e94a" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303854 1034 "(0,-1)" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303854 1111 #uuid "c8517b9d-cb03-5233-bae1-ddec7f803455" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303855 1034 "(0,2)" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303855 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303855 1111 #uuid "ad8c0bfb-c570-56df-abe4-7d63bcedb5b7" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303856 1034 "(0,-2)" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303856 1111 #uuid "9de1b6e4-ab5f-5e3f-bffa-3c85aa9ec6b7" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303857 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303858 13194139534695 true] [17592186303857 1089 "q-304068" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303857 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534695 true] [17592186303857 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{3x+2}{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(-1,-1).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303857 1113 #uuid "53f492bb-7406-5e44-8b31-b4ebc75fe4ea" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303857 1145 "Let $f(x)=\\frac{3x+2}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3x+2}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{-2}-4{x}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(-1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =-\\frac{3}{(-1)^{2}}-\\frac{4}{(-1)^{3}} \\\\  & =-3+4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=1$ and the coordinates of our point $(-1,-1),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-1) & =1\\cdot (x-(-1)) \\\\ y+1 & =x+1 \\\\ y & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303859 13194139534695 true] [17592186303858 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534695 true] [17592186303858 1041 "field-1" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303858 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303859 13194139534695 true] [17592186303858 1110 #uuid "80e66cda-021b-5e9c-8a7c-557c0808ab21" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303859 1034 "x" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303859 1111 #uuid "603c4794-acf6-5532-8946-c429a61b215f" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303861 13194139534695 true] [17592186303860 1089 "q-342350" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303860 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534695 true] [17592186303860 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=2x-{x}^{3}$ at the point  $(1,1).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303860 1113 #uuid "cc861208-317d-5f52-876e-9120cd395379" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303860 1145 "Let $f(x)=2x-{x}^{3}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2-3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(1)=2-3({1}^{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-1$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,1),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =(-1)(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1+1 \\\\ y & =-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303862 13194139534695 true] [17592186303861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303863 13194139534695 true] [17592186303861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534695 true] [17592186303861 1041 "field-1" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303862 13194139534695 true] [17592186303861 1110 #uuid "cacdcdca-e5f1-5aac-b5df-1c81368c6246" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303862 1034 "-x+2" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303862 1111 #uuid "cb0c79ba-e8ce-57c8-b48e-156e9659f61e" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303863 1034 "x" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534695 true] [17592186303863 1111 #uuid "c5f596cf-8d6b-5f5d-8b56-584603f8a7e2" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303865 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303867 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1089 "q-342380" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1100 "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point  $(4,-4)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1113 #uuid "98faba34-f4b8-5f9c-951f-5cba695daf64" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303864 1145 "Let $f(x)=-2\\sqrt{x}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-4) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-4) \\\\ y+4 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2-4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}(0)-2 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,-2).$" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303866 13194139534695 true] [17592186303865 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534695 true] [17592186303865 1041 "field-1" 13194139534695 true] [17592186303865 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303866 13194139534695 true] [17592186303865 1110 #uuid "334e1ada-a5bf-5543-9127-2d44edd54566" 1319